kind: perf

The hill climb that finds a large convex's support point (getShapeSupportLog,
every convex past 32 vertices) cost far more than its few steps:
- its warm-start table was skipped whenever the last direction was zero, which
  MinkowskiDiff::set makes it for every new pair, so each pair's first climb
  started at vertex 0 and crossed the hull; and a turn of the direction
  replaced the hint with the table's best even when the hint was better
- the table took 14 dot products to consult, on every sharp turn
- it cleared a visited flag for every vertex on every call, so each climb
  cost the whole hull however short it was
Now the table is a cube map, the vertex farthest along the middle of each of
16 by 16 cells on each face of a cube (indices only, 6 KB a hull), built
where the 14 were, and each call starts from the better of the hint and its
direction's cell: two dot products, as MuJoCo seeds its own climb from a
27-direction grid (engine_collision_convex.c). More cells kept shortening
the climb up to 16 a side on robot and ellipsoid hulls of 42 to 2562
vertices: 27 cells to 1536 took distances on g1's 724-vertex (median) hulls
from 509 to 344 us. A vertex is visited when its 64-bit stamp is the call's,
which only grows, so nothing is ever cleared.
The climb visits as it did, so it returns a vertex as far along the
direction; only where several are equally far may it name another.
The flags the climb used are left to the one function that still reads them
(getShapeSupportSetLog, which now sizes them itself, as the climb did for
it), so MinkowskiDiff::set no longer clears them for every pair.
Measured on robot hulls, one core, every non-adjacent pair, trimkit 0.3.0
with its GJK starting between the hulls' centers, us per configuration:
distances 1187 -> 633 (talos) and 924 -> 344 (g1), collides 58 -> 31 and
62 -> 23 (check/bench/collision/mujoco.coal.notes.md). Covered by
check/tests/test_collision.py and check/bench/collision/trimkit_robot.py's
distance against exact triangle distance between the hulls.
Not reported upstream yet.

